            "id": "4954971",
            "title": "What Moved Markets This Week",
            "description": "<html><body><div class=\"wsb_wrapper\"> <div class=\"wsb_main\"><span><p data-eci=\"true\"><strong>Listen on the go! A daily podcast of Wall Street Breakfast will be available by 8:00 a.m. on <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/author/wall-street-breakfast?utm_source=newsletter&amp;utm_medium=toptext&amp;utm_campaign=wsbpodpromo\">Seeking Alpha</a>, <a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/wall-street-breakfast/id1358381502\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">iTunes</a>, <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/show/05uLjJxkVgQsRk8LWLCLpx\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Spotify</a>.</strong></p></span></div> <figure class=\"getty-figure\" data-type=\"getty-image\"><picture><img alt=\"\" data-id=\"173024040\" data-type=\"getty-image\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"1024\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 132px), (max-width: 1199px) calc(100vw - 666px), (max-width: 1307px) calc(100vw - 708px), 600px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w630\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w1536 1536w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w1280 1280w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w1080 1080w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w750 750w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w640 640w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w480 480w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w320 320w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/173024040/image_173024040.jpg?io=getty-c-w240 240w\" width=\"1536\"/><figcaption><p class=\"item-credits\">narvikk/E+ via Getty Images</p></figcaption></picture></figure>\n<p class=\"wsb_bold\" data-skip-content-styles=\"\"> </p> <p><span class=\"b italic\">Up for a challenge? Test your knowledge on the biggest events in the investing world over the past week. Take the latest <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/quiz/73-investment-news-quiz-friday-oct-16-2026-10-16\">Seeking Alpha News Quiz</a> and see how you stack up against the competition.</span></p> <h2> </h2> <p><br/>Wall Street closed the week mixed as a sharp spike in volatility reflected fresh tech struggles, while investors continued to digest hotter-than-expected CPI data and the latest bank earnings.<br/><br/>CPI inflation <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4652866-cpi-inflation-heats-up-in-september-in-line-with-expectations\" target=\"_blank\">heated up</a> in September. On a year-over-year basis, the Consumer Price Index rose 3.7%, matching the consensus forecast and accelerating from a 3.4% gain in August.<br/><br/>The Cboe Volatility Index (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/VIX\" title=\"S&amp;P VIX Index\">VIX</a>) surged roughly 30% on Friday afternoon to trade above 21, reaching a more than <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4653956-wall-street-fear-gauge-vix-surges-to-over-four-month-high\" target=\"_blank\">four-month high</a> as tech stocks continued to struggle.<br/><br/>Big banks kicked off <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4651821-watch-big-banks-capital-markets-commercial-banking-results-in-q3-earnings\" target=\"_blank\">Q3 earnings</a> season as traders digested results from Goldman Sachs (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/GS\" title=\"The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc.\">GS</a>), JPMorgan (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/JPM\" title=\"JPMorgan Chase &amp; Co.\">JPM</a>), Citigroup (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/C\" title=\"Citigroup Inc.\">C</a>), Wells Fargo (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/WFC\" title=\"Wells Fargo &amp; Company\">WFC</a>), and other major lenders.<br/><br/>For the week, the blue-chip Dow (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/DJI\" title=\"Dow Jones Industrial Average Index\">DJI</a>) added <span class=\"green\">+0.67%</span>, the benchmark S&amp;P (<a class=\"ticker-link\" href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SP500\">SP500</a>) lost <span class=\"red\">-1.95%</span>, and the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/C\" title=\"Citigroup Inc.\">C</a>OMP:IND) plunged <span class=\"red\">-4.48%</span>. Read a preview of next week's major events in <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4653857-catalyst-watch-meta-earnings-kroger-event-and-black-monday-turns-39\" target=\"_blank\">Seeking Alpha's Catalyst Watch.</a><br/> </p> <h2><a class=\"!no-underline !text-share-text\" href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4653834-fed-data-reveals-1-in-5-americans-are-falling-behind-on-debt\">Behind on the bills</a></h2> <p>The U.S. government isn't the only one with a debt problem. 1 in 5 Americans fell behind on a loan or mortgage payment in 2025, according to new data from the Federal Reserve. That figure is up from 1 in 8 Americans in 2022 and marks the highest level since 2007. Why is it happening, and what will it mean for the economy? <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4653834-fed-data-reveals-1-in-5-americans-are-falling-behind-on-debt\"><span class=\"b\">Read more.</span></a></p> <p class=\"wsb_bold\" data-skip-content-styles=\"\">Seeking Alpha's Calls Of The Week</p> <p><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4953988-jpmorgan-chase-q3-earnings-top-tier-bank-stock-reflect-it\">JPMorgan Chase Q3 2026: A Top-Tier Bank Whose Shares Already Reflect It</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4952839-nike-taught-me-a-dividend-lesson-and-a-china-lesson-rating-downgrade\">Nike Taught Me A Dividend Lesson And A China Lesson</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4953530-viatris-is-the-pacira-deal-a-game-changer-rating-upgrade\">Viatris: Is The Pacira Deal A Game Changer?</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4952667-marvell-investor-day-resets-the-ai-growth-story\">Marvell: Investor Day Resets The AI Growth Story</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4952688-mcdonalds-same-store-sales-are-an-overrated-metric-upgrade\">McDonald's: Same-Store Sales Are An Overrated Metric</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4953338-palantir-i-couldnt-have-been-more-wrong-i-see-the-light-now-buy\">Palantir: I Couldn't Have Been More Wrong, I See The Light Now - Buy</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4953016-lockheed-martin-strong-buy-not-for-obvious-reasons\">Lockheed Martin: Strong Buy, But Not For The Obvious Reasons</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4952811-lumen-13-5-billion-in-debt-is-too-much-for-an-ai-bear-market-rating-downgrade\">Lumen: $13.5 Billion In Debt Is Too Much For An AI Bear Market</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4952811-lumen-13-5-billion-in-debt-is-too-much-for-an-ai-bear-market-rating-downgrade\">Novavax: Sell The False Plague Breakout</a><br/><br/><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4953526-micron-more-for-longer\">Micron: More For Longer</a><br/><br/> </p> <p class=\"wsb_bold\" data-skip-content-styles=\"\">Weekly Movement</p> <p><span><strong>U.S. Indices</strong><br/>Dow <span class=\"green\">+0.7%</span> to 52,002. S&amp;P 500 <span class=\"red\">-2%</span> to 7,659. Nasdaq <span class=\"red\">-4.5%</span> to 26,140. Russell 2000 <span class=\"red\">-3.1%</span> to 2,721. CBOE Volatility Index <span class=\"green\">+34.7%</span> to 19.99. <br/><br/><strong>S&amp;P 500 Sectors</strong><br/>Consumer Staples <span class=\"green\">+5%</span>. Utilities <span class=\"green\">+2%</span>. Financials <span class=\"green\">+1.4%</span>. Telecom <span class=\"red\">-1.6%</span>. Healthcare <span c